# Template for flash/flash.cfg — the 56800E Flash Programmer's (fflash.exe)
# configuration file. Confirmed from the "56800E Flash Programmer User's
# Guide" (Rev. 0, 09/2005): fflash takes a config file rather than
# command-line flags for target device and debug interface selection.
#
# CodeWarrior ships real, per-device .cfg templates under an
# "initialization" folder, historically at a path shaped like:
#   {CodeWarrior install}\M56800E Support\initialization\
# Copy the one matching your board's exact device variant (see chip
# silkscreen, e.g. MC56F83789) into flash/flash.cfg — don't hand-write
# this from scratch, the same way we don't hand-write the linker .cmd file
# (see README "Important note on src/ and linker/").
#
# What's confirmed from the manual so far:
#   - fflash defaults to "the current configured device on the CCS server"
#     unless overridden
#   - -USB overrides to use the USB interface (this is the OSBDM path)
#   - -LPT<n> / -p<PORT> select a parallel-port Command Converter (legacy,
#     not applicable to this board's on-board USB OSBDM)
# What's NOT yet confirmed (verify against your installed manual, usually
# under {CodeWarrior install}\Help\, before relying on it):
#   - whether there's a dedicated run/reset-after-program flag, or whether
#     "run after flash" is a setting inside the .cfg file itself
#   - the exact device-name string this .cfg expects for MC56F83xxx parts
